# Pre/Post Scripts — All Three Languages

The same pattern written in JavaScript, Python, and Shell: a `pre_script` pushes an `X-Script-Lang` header and stores it as a runtime variable, then a `post_script` reads it back from httpbin's echoed response and asserts it via `voiden.assert` (script-based assertions, as opposed to the declarative `assertions-table` used elsewhere in this repo).

```void
---
type: request-separator
attrs:
  uid: "13b47570-177d-48e9-ba57-d6820cdeaf5d"
  colorIndex: 0
  label: "JavaScript"
---
```

```void
